{"analysis":"Version 0 got positive and negative recall high, but 130 of 325 neutral texts went to positive (65) or negative (65). Its rule told the model to label overall emotional tone even when the brand is not named, and that contradicts the dataset description. The annotators mark sentiment towards the brand, product or service. Neutral is the large default class.

Neutral texts mislabelled positive include:
- thanks for an answer or fix ('Díky za odpověď', 'Děkuju za vyjasnění');
- hopes and wishes ('snad se v Opavě dočkáme :)', 'Doufám že to projde');
- saying you ordered or own something ('Už mám objednáno =)');
- contest entries and wanting prizes;
- happy chat about one's own life;
- brand promo text;
- praise of things that are not the brand ('Lednice je nádherná').

Neutral texts mislabelled negative include:
- mild regret or sad smileys about circumstances ('nestíháme... :(', 'nám chybí pouze jeden..:((');
- requests and suggestions ('Chci levnější volání...', 'by to chtělo připojení');
- teasing or arguing with other users;
- neutral fault reports and questions with '??';
- dry irony that is not a clear attack on the brand.

Fix: make the target 'opinion about the page's brand, product or service', and make neutral the default when no such clear evaluation exists. Emoticons, thanks, hopes, wishes and requests do not count by themselves. Keep clear complaints (switching provider, overpriced, sarcastic mockery of an offer) and clear praise (loyalty, cute zoo animals, loving the product) as before, since recall on those was strong. Add a few real borderline examples to show where each boundary lies.","question":"Does this Czech Facebook post express a clear opinion about the page's brand, product or service: positive (praise, love, delight with it), negative (complaint, criticism, mockery of it), or neutral (no clear evaluation of the brand)?","rule":"Judge only the opinion about the brand, its products, ads, animals or service, not the general mood or the emoticons. Neutral is the default and covers several kinds of post: thanks for an answer or fix, hopes and wishes, requests and suggestions, contest entries, saying you bought or own something, chat or teasing between users, own-life stories, and praise or sadness about things other than the brand. Mild regret about circumstances also stays neutral ('nestíháme :('). Negative needs a clear complaint, criticism or sarcasm aimed at the brand. Positive needs clear praise, delight or loyalty towards the brand or its products.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Explicit praise or enthusiasm about the brand's products, ads, animals, staff or service, and loyalty statements.","examples":["já mám o2 13 let a neměnila bych (I've had O2 for 13 years and wouldn't switch)","Jaký je ňuňatýý! :)) (How cute it is!)","Kam se hrabou reklamy na T Mobile :D (T-Mobile's ads can't compare)"],"cues":"skvělé (great), úžasné (amazing), miluju (I love), nejlepší (best), doporučuju (I recommend), chutná (tastes good)","not_for":"Thanks for an answer ('Díky za odpověď'), hopes ('snad se dočkáme :)'), 'Už mám objednáno =)' (Already ordered), wanting a prize, and praise of non-brand things are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Questions, information, requests, suggestions, plain fault reports, thanks, hopes, contest chatter, user banter, jokes, and feelings not aimed at the brand.","examples":["Už mám objednáno =) (I've already ordered)","Díky za odpověď. Tak to to na rozsvícení bohužel nestíháme... :( (Thanks for the reply. Unfortunately we won't make it to the lighting...)","Chci levnější volání, 3G pokrytí, Internet bez cenzury a bez FUP. (I want cheaper calls, 3G coverage, internet without censorship and without FUP.)","Lednice je nádherná a rozsáhlá zahrada (Lednice is a beautiful, large garden)"],"cues":"díky za odpověď (thanks for the reply), doufám (I hope), snad (hopefully), prosím (please), mě by se hodily (I could use), jak (how), :) or :( without an evaluation of the brand","not_for":"Clear frustration with the brand ('už mě to přestává bavit' (I'm getting fed up)) is negative; clear love of its products is positive."},"negative":{"what":"Clear complaints or criticism of the brand: price, service, quality, removed products, threats to leave, sarcasm or mockery of its offers.","examples":["Jdu si do trafiky pro simku konkurence, už mě to přestává bavit. (I'm going to get a competitor's SIM, I'm getting fed up.)","FUP 2 GB za 333,-Kč :-))))) už dlouho mě tak nikdo nepobavil (FUP 2 GB for 333 CZK, nobody has amused me this much in ages)","bez prasátka to už neni ono :D (without the piggy it's not the same)"],"cues":"předražený (overpriced), nefunguje (doesn't work), odejdu (I'll leave), konkurence (competitor), zklamal (disappointed), fuj (yuck), už nikdy (never again)","not_for":"Suggestions, wishes for better offers, neutral fault questions, sad smileys about one's own situation, and arguing with other users are neutral."}}}

