Fix: make the target 'opinion about the page's brand, product or service', and make neutral the default when no such clear evaluation exists. Emoticons, thanks, hopes, wishes and requests do not count by themselves. Keep clear complaints (switching provider, overpriced, sarcastic mockery of an offer) and clear praise (loyalty, cute zoo animals, loving the product) as before, since recall on those was strong. Add a few real borderline examples to show where each boundary lies. The previous draft went 1 word over the limit, so this version shortens the wording and drops the Lednice example from neutral, while keeping 'non-brand praise' in the rule.","question":"Does this Czech Facebook post express a clear opinion about the page's brand, product or service: positive (praise, love, delight with it), negative (complaint, criticism, mockery of it), or neutral (no clear evaluation of the brand)?","rule":"Judge only the opinion about the brand, its products, ads, animals or service, not the general mood or emoticons. Neutral is the default and covers several kinds of post: thanks for an answer or fix, hopes and wishes, requests and suggestions, contest entries, saying you bought or own something, user banter, own-life stories, and praise or sadness about non-brand things. Mild regret about circumstances also stays neutral. Negative needs a clear complaint, criticism or sarcasm aimed at the brand. Positive needs clear praise, delight or loyalty towards the brand or its products.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Explicit praise or enthusiasm about the brand's products, ads, animals, staff or service, and loyalty statements.","examples":["já mám o2 13 let a neměnila bych (I've had O2 for 13 years and wouldn't switch)","Jaký je ňuňatýý! :)) (How cute it is!)","Kam se hrabou reklamy na T Mobile :D (T-Mobile's ads can't compare)"],"cues":"skvělé (great), úžasné (amazing), miluju (I love), nejlepší (best), doporučuju (I recommend), chutná (tastes good)","not_for":"Thanks for an answer ('Díky za odpověď'), hopes ('snad se dočkáme :)'), 'Už mám objednáno =)' (Already ordered), wanting a prize, and praise of non-brand things are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Questions, information, requests, suggestions, plain fault reports, thanks, hopes, contest chatter, user banter, jokes, and feelings not aimed at the brand.","examples":["Už mám objednáno =) (I've already ordered)","Díky za odpověď. Tak to to na rozsvícení bohužel nestíháme... :( (Thanks for the reply. Unfortunately we won't make it to the lighting...)","Chci levnější volání, 3G pokrytí, Internet bez cenzury a bez FUP. (I want cheaper calls, 3G coverage, internet without censorship and without FUP.)"],"cues":"díky za odpověď (thanks for the reply), doufám (I hope), snad (hopefully), prosím (please), mě by se hodily (I could use), jak (how), :) or :( without an evaluation of the brand","not_for":"Clear frustration with the brand ('už mě to přestává bavit' (I'm getting fed up)) is negative; clear love of its products is positive."},"negative":{"what":"Clear complaints or criticism of the brand: price, service, quality, removed products, threats to leave, sarcasm or mockery of its offers.","examples":["Jdu si do trafiky pro simku konkurence, už mě to přestává bavit. (I'm going to get a competitor's SIM, I'm getting fed up.)","FUP 2 GB za 333,-Kč :-))))) už dlouho mě tak nikdo nepobavil (FUP 2 GB for 333 CZK, nobody has amused me this much in ages)","bez prasátka to už neni ono :D (without the piggy it's not the same)"],"cues":"předražený (overpriced), nefunguje (doesn't work), odejdu (I'll leave), konkurence (competitor), zklamal (disappointed), fuj (yuck), už nikdy (never again)","not_for":"Suggestions, wishes for better offers, neutral fault questions, sad smileys about one's own situation, and arguing with other users are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 1 overcorrected. Restricting sentiment to the brand pushed 62 positive texts and 30 negative texts into neutral, and macro-F1 fell from 76.6 to 73.0.

The gold labels show that the annotators do count tone not aimed at the brand.

Positive texts that went to neutral:
- thanks ('Díky za odpověď :-)', 'děkuji za info', 'Děkuji mnohokrát');
- good wishes and congratulations ('všechno nejlepší', 'Držím pěsti!!!', 'krásný den i vám!!!');
- wanting the product ('Dal bych si :P', 'je já chci taky..:)', 'hned bych si dal');
- delight ('krásné sněhové ráno..! :)', 'Jejda mane,to je micánek').

Negative texts that went to neutral:
- sadness or frustration with crying emoticons ('Chudák kočka', 'Nevolááá :((((', 'zase jsem to nestih :-(');
- insults to other users ('ty osle');
- pointed 'why don't you' complaints.

So I return to version 0's emotional-tone framing, which got positive and negative right, and tighten neutral using version 0's errors. A plain smiley or :D on a factual, chatty or joking line is not enough for positive; a feeling word, thanks, wish or desire is needed. Questions, requests, suggestions, wishlists of better tariffs, flat fault reports, banter or teasing jokes, ironic asides without a sad or angry marker, and promo text are neutral. Hope alone ('snad', 'doufám') is neutral unless combined with thanks or delight. Negative needs an explicit complaint, sadness marker, insult or sarcastic attack.","question":"What feeling does this Czech Facebook comment express: positive (thanks, wishes, praise, delight, wanting the product), negative (complaint, sadness, frustration, insult, sarcastic attack), or neutral (factual, questioning, joking or chatty with no clear feeling)?","rule":"Annotators label the expressed feeling even when the brand is not the target: thanks, congratulations, good wishes, delight and craving a product are positive, while sadness, frustration, complaints and insults to other users are negative. A smiley or :D alone does not make a text positive or negative; it needs a feeling word, thanks, wish, sad emoticon like :( or :(((, or a clear complaint. Questions, requests, suggestions, wished-for tariffs, flat fault reports, banter, teasing jokes, mild irony, hopes ('snad', 'doufám') and promo-style statements are neutral.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Thanks, congratulations, good wishes, praise of products, ads, animals or photos, delight, loyalty, and wanting or buying the product with enthusiasm.","examples":["Díky za odpověď :-) (Thanks for the answer)","Držím pěsti!!! (Fingers crossed!!!)","Dal bych si :P (I'd have some)","Jejda mane,to je micánek :) :) (Oh man, what a kitty)"],"cues":"děkuji, díky (thank you), všechno nejlepší (all the best), držím pěsti (fingers crossed), super, krásné (beautiful), dal bych si (I'd have some), chci taky (I want one too), jůů (yay)","not_for":"Factual or chatty lines with only a smiley ('Už je hotový :D' (it's done now :D)), hopes ('snad se v Opavě dočkáme :)' (hopefully we'll get it in Opava)), and promo text are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Questions, information, requests, suggestions, plain problem reports, user banter, jokes, mild irony and hopes without a clear feeling word.","examples":["jak deaktivuji službu Útrata?? (how do I deactivate the Útrata service??)","Chci levnější volání, 3G pokrytí, Internet bez cenzury a bez FUP. (I want cheaper calls, 3G coverage, internet without censorship and without FUP.)","Už mám objednáno =) (I've already ordered)","jen jestli ondra není netbot, na určitý typ otázky vždy stejná odpověď :-D (I wonder if Ondra isn't a netbot, always the same answer to a certain type of question)"],"cues":"jak (how), proč (why) in plain questions, prosím (please), snad (hopefully), doufám (I hope), kdyby (if), :D in banter","not_for":"Questions loaded with sad or angry markers ('já mám vynulované skore :((((( nevíte proč???' (my score has been reset, does anyone know why???)) are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Complaints about price, service or product, threats to leave, sarcasm or mockery, insults to other users, and sad or frustrated remarks.","examples":["Jdu si do trafiky pro simku konkurence, už mě to přestává bavit. (I'm going to get a competitor's SIM, I'm getting fed up.)","zase jsem to nestih, poslední dobou mi skoro pokaždý tyhle bomba akce utečou přímo před očima :-( (I missed it again; lately these great deals nearly always slip away right in front of me)","Chudák kočka,....:-/ (Poor cat)"],"cues":"předražený (overpriced), nefunguje (doesn't work), už nikdy (never again), škoda (pity), chudák (poor thing), ty vole (dude, as a swear), osel (donkey, as an insult), :( , :(((, :-/","not_for":"Flat fault reports or questions without frustration markers, and light teasing between users, are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 2 scored 79.0. Positive recall is good (142/155) and so is negative (109/120), but 102 neutral texts still go to positive (51) or negative (51).

Neutral texts the model labels positive:
- courtesy thanks closing a question or request ('...jak se dovíme...? Děkuji za info.', 'předem díky za info', 'Díky moc' after asking for points);
- thanks closing an explanation ('Ano myslela jsem to tak... Díky za odpověď');
- contest entries and prize wishes ('mě by se hodily tři', 'Taky potřebuji.. ID', 'dala bych to detičkám');
- descriptive statements about the product or own life with a smiley;
- praise of non-brand places;
- agreement with another user ('Svatá pravda Ondřeji').

Neutral texts the model labels negative:
- factual reports containing 'bohužel', 'škoda' or a single :( ('takže si to bohužel kontrolovat nemůžeme', 'nám chybí pouze jeden..:((', 'Díky za odpověď... nestíháme :(');
- argumentative or ironic replies to other users without a direct insult;
- flat fault reports and questions with ??? or !!!;
- noting a change in taste.

Changes:
- Thanks is positive only when it is the main message; thanks used as a closing formula after a question, request or explanation is neutral.
- Contest or prize requests are neutral.
- 'bohužel' or 'škoda' in a factual line is neutral; negative needs real frustration, a complaint, an insult or a sarcastic attack on the brand.
- Arguing with users without name-calling is neutral.

Keep craving the product ('Dal bych si'), wishes and standalone thanks as positive, so positive recall should hold.","question":"What feeling does this Czech Facebook comment express: positive (thanks, wishes, praise, delight, craving the product), negative (complaint, frustration, sadness, insult, sarcastic attack), or neutral (factual, asking, requesting, joking or chatty with no clear feeling)?","rule":"Positive needs feeling as the main message: standalone thanks, congratulations, good wishes, praise or craving the product. Thanks closing a question, request or explanation, prize or contest requests, agreement with users, and smiley-decorated statements of fact are neutral. Negative needs real frustration, a complaint, an insult, crying emoticons, or sarcasm against the brand. 'bohužel', 'škoda' or one :( in a factual note, flat fault reports, questions with ??? and arguing with users without name-calling are neutral.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Standalone thanks, congratulations, good wishes, praise of products, ads, animals or photos, delight, loyalty, and craving the product.","examples":["Díky za odpověď :-) (Thanks for the answer)","Držím pěsti!!! (Fingers crossed!!!)","Dal bych si :P (I'd have some)","Jejda mane,to je micánek :) :) (Oh man, what a kitty)"],"cues":"děkuji, díky as the whole message (thank you), všechno nejlepší (all the best), držím pěsti (fingers crossed), super, krásné (beautiful), dal bych si (I'd have some), jůů (yay)","not_for":"'Chtěl bych se Vás zeptat, jak se dovíme, jestli jsme vyhráli přívěšek nebo ne? Děkuji za info.' (I'd like to ask how we find out whether we won the pendant or not? Thanks for the info.) and 'mě by se hodily tři' (I could use three) are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Questions, requests, contest entries, information, plain fault reports, user banter or arguing, jokes, hopes, and factual notes with mild regret.","examples":["jak deaktivuji službu Útrata?? (how do I deactivate the Útrata service??)","takže si to bohužel kontrolovat nemůžeme... (so unfortunately we can't check it...)","Taky potřebuji.. ID: 1677222513 (I need it too.. ID: 1677222513)","Chci levnější volání, 3G pokrytí, Internet bez cenzury a bez FUP. (I want cheaper calls, 3G coverage, internet without censorship and without FUP.)"],"cues":"jak (how), kde (where), prosím (please), předem díky (thanks in advance), snad (hopefully), doufám (I hope), bohužel (unfortunately) in plain reports, :D in banter","not_for":"Fed-up complaints, crying ':(((' outbursts, and name-calling are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Complaints about price, service or product, threats to leave, sarcasm or mockery of the brand, insults, and sad or frustrated outbursts.","examples":["Jdu si do trafiky pro simku konkurence, už mě to přestává bavit. (I'm going to get a competitor's SIM, I'm getting fed up.)","zase jsem to nestih, poslední dobou mi skoro pokaždý tyhle bomba akce utečou přímo před očima :-( (I missed it again; lately these great deals nearly always slip away right in front of me)","Chudák kočka,....:-/ (Poor cat)"],"cues":"předražený (overpriced), už nikdy (never again), už mě to nebaví (I'm fed up), chudák (poor thing), ty vole (dude, as a swear), osel (donkey, as an insult), :(((","not_for":"Factual problem reports, mild 'bohužel', and ironic but polite replies to other users are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 3 scored 80.5. Neutral precision improved (neutral→positive fell from 51 to 22), but positive recall dropped from 142 to 124 and negative recall from 109 to 101.

Positive texts that went to neutral:
- thanks that are not attached to a request, even inside an informative message ('už mi mail dorazil, děkuji :-)', 'E-mail je: ... Mockrát Vám děkuji :)', 'Děkuji za reakci... ještě jednou děkuji', 'Díky, Anděl mám znatelně blíž :)');
- happy short updates about buying, having or visiting with a smiley ('Nakoupeno :)', 'už je mám na cestě :-)', 'my byli v neděli v solné jeskyni :-)', 'jj sou to sestřičky ;-)))');
- mild praise ('mě chutnalo ;)', 'je dobrej :-D', 'vtipné', 'Sdílím je jedinečné :)').

Negative texts that went to neutral:
- disappointment with :( or :/ about missing out or unavailability ('škoda,že u nás prší :/', 'nikde ... není :(', 'přišel pozdě..:-(', 'nevěřím ... výhře:(');
- 'why did you stop / why don't you' questions about brand decisions ('Zajímalo by mě z jakých důvodů se už nenabízí...', 'Proč máte nastavené mazání...');
- resigned complaints ('cekani kolem 1hodiny bohuzel normalni').

The remaining neutral→negative errors are mostly banter, irony and teasing between users, flat fault reports and price facts.

Changes:
- Restore thanks as positive unless it closes a question or request.
- Treat cheerful personal updates with a smiley and mild praise as positive.
- Treat disappointment with :( or :/ and questions objecting to brand decisions as negative.
- Keep information questions, requests, contest entries, flat fault reports, user banter and teasing, promo text and jokes neutral.","question":"What feeling does this Czech Facebook comment express: positive (thanks, wishes, praise, delight, craving or happily buying the product), negative (complaint, disappointment, frustration, insult, sarcastic attack), or neutral (factual, asking, requesting, joking or bantering with no clear feeling)?","rule":"Thanks is positive unless it only closes a question or request ('...? Děkuji za info'). Cheerful updates with a smiley, mild praise and good wishes are positive too. Disappointment with :( or :/ about missing out, unavailability, waiting or price, and questions objecting to a brand decision are negative. Information questions, requests, contest entries, flat fault reports, teasing or ironic banter between users without name-calling, promo text and jokes are neutral.","criteria":{"positive":{"what":"Thanks, congratulations, wishes, praise (even mild), delight, loyalty, craving the product, and cheerful updates about buying, having or visiting.","examples":["už mi mail dorazil, děkuji :-) (the email has arrived, thank you)","Nakoupeno :) (Bought)","mě chutnalo ;) (I liked the taste)","Dal bych si :P (I'd have some)"],"cues":"děkuji, díky (thank you), všechno nejlepší (all the best), držím pěsti (fingers crossed), chutnalo (tasted good), dobrej (good), super, krásné (beautiful), jůů (yay)","not_for":"Thanks closing a question ('Chtěl bych se Vás zeptat, jak se dovíme... Děkuji za info.' (I'd like to ask how we find out... Thanks for the info.)), contest requests ('mě by se hodily tři' (I could use three)), and promo text are neutral."},"neutral":{"what":"Information questions, requests, contest entries, facts, flat fault reports, user banter and teasing, jokes, and hopes.","examples":["jak deaktivuji službu Útrata?? (how do I deactivate the Útrata service??)","Taky potřebuji.. ID: 1677222513 (I need it too.. ID: 1677222513)","jen jestli ondra není netbot, na určitý typ otázky vždy stejná odpověď :-D (I wonder if Ondra isn't a netbot, always the same answer to a certain type of question)","Tak nakonec je to 25 kč samozřejmně s Vaším DPH.. (So in the end it's 25 CZK, of course with your VAT..)"],"cues":"jak (how), kde (where), prosím (please), předem díky (thanks in advance), ID, :D in banter","not_for":"Disappointment with :( or :/, objecting 'why' questions, and fed-up complaints are negative."},"negative":{"what":"Complaints, disappointment about missing out or unavailability, objections to brand decisions, threats to leave, sarcasm, and insults.","examples":["Jdu si do trafiky pro simku konkurence, už mě to přestává bavit. (I'm going to get a competitor's SIM, I'm getting fed up.)","Taky jsme sháněli pěnoknír ale nikde v okolí Moravské Třebové snad není :( (We were looking for the foam moustache too but there isn't any around Moravská Třebová :()","Zajímalo by mě¨z jakých důvodů se už nenabízí Chciken burgery.. (I wonder why Chicken burgers are no longer offered..)"],"cues":"předražený (overpriced), už nikdy (never again), škoda (pity), nestih (missed it), už neni ono (it's not the same), proč už ne (why not anymore), osel (donkey, as an insult), :( , :/","not_for":"Flat fault reports, price facts, and joking or ironic replies to other users are neutral."}}}

{"analysis":"Version 4 brought back version 0's behaviour: positive recall 152/155 and negative 113/120, but 128 neutral texts went to positive or negative, and macro-F1 fell to 77.3.

The broad cues I added caused most of the damage:
- 'cheerful updates with a smiley are positive' (wrong for 'Už je hotový :D', 'akurát pijem :)', 'Praha -Černý most :-)');
- 'disappointment with :( is negative' (wrong for 'nám chybí pouze jeden..:((', 'Proto jsem dnes raději ten internet nevyužívala :-(');
